# ReluLayer™ Root Cursor Rules — Authoritative Agent Governance

> This is the workspace-level `.cursorrules` for the ReluLayer™ primary monorepo. It governs every agent interaction. The canonical product baseline is `PRD.md` in this repository. For entity identifiers, refer to `Organizations/AtelierLogicGroup/00-governance/entity-identity.md`.

## 1. Identity, Role & Product Framing

- You are operating on **ReluLayer™**, a deterministic **Edge Governor** and **Execution Gatekeeper** for autonomous AI agents, LLM tool calling, and Physical Super Intelligence (Physical SI) actuator loops.
- The kernel is pure `#![no_std]` Rust; probabilistic layers may plan, but ReluLayer™ authorizes execution deterministically.
- Do not anthropomorphize the kernel. Avoid words like "reflexes", "thoughts", "instincts", or "believes".

## 2. Author Provenance & Commit Attribution

- Every commit must be authored by:
  ```text
  ishmaelamin <ishmael.amin@outlook.com>
  ```
- Strictly prohibited in any commit message or trailer:
  - `Co-authored-by: Cursor`
  - `Co-authored-by: GitHub Copilot`
  - Any bot, assistant, or automated-author attribution.
- Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):
  - `docs(prd): ...`
  - `feat(core): ...`
  - `fix(security): ...`
  - `ci(actions): ...`

## 3. Dual-Repository Parity

- `/home/iamin/Dist/relulayer-oss` (public mirror) and `/home/iamin/Organizations/ReluLayer` (primary monorepo) must remain synchronized for all files that exist in both workspaces.
- When you modify `PRD.md` or `.cursorrules` in one repository, mirror the identical content to the other before pushing.
- The public mirror is the open-core wedge only. Never copy proprietary monorepo content (`pendulum_sim.rs`, `veristate`, `20-pilots-and-proposals/`, `AtelierLogicGroup/`) into the public mirror.

## 4. Architectural Non-Negotiables

- `#![no_std]` first for all safety-critical crates.
- Zero dynamic heap allocations on authorization / hot paths.
- Bounded stack allocations must stay < 1 KB per call.
- Sub-microsecond latency ceiling for the micro-action fast path.
- Production builds use `panic = "abort"`, `lto = true`, `opt-level = 3`.
- Embedded targets: trap `_sbrk` to `ENOMEM`; no global allocator.

## 5. PyO3 & FFI Contract

- Action identifiers and payloads are raw `bytes` (`&[u8]` in Rust, `bytes` in Python).
- Verification failures raise `ValueError` in Python or return a negative FFI code.
- Never design the API so that authorization success/failure is returned as a plain boolean that can be ignored.
- Use PyO3 0.23+ smart-pointer signatures (`&Bound<'_, PyModule>`).

## 6. Nomenclature & Branding

- Product name: **ReluLayer™**.
- Categories: **Edge Governor**, **Execution Gatekeeper**.
- Federal / defense references: **Physical Super Intelligence (Physical SI)**.
- Entity: **Atelier Logic Group LLC dba ReluLayer™** — CAGE `20JX8`, UEI `G9WFN3AL69J3`.

## 7. SCM & Index Discipline

- Stage explicit paths only. `git add .`, `git add -A`, and `git add *` are forbidden.
- Never commit `target/`, `node_modules/`, `.venv/`, build artifacts, transient caches, compiled dynamic libraries, or Windows `Zone.Identifier` files.
- Verify `git status` is clean after every commit.
- Before pushing, run `git diff --stat` and confirm only intended files are included.

## 8. Safety-Critical Code Style

- Prefer deterministic algorithms over probabilistic heuristics on the hot path.
- Static stack arrays only; no `Vec`, `Box`, or `HashMap` in `#![no_std]` paths.
- All arithmetic in `relulayer-core` embedded target uses Q16.16 fixed-point or carefully bounded `f32`; never `f64` in the bare-metal kernel.
- Symplectic auditor invariant: `det(J) == 1.0` within tolerance where applicable.

## 9. Documentation & Traceability

- `PRD.md` is the authoritative source of truth. Engineering changes must be traceable to it.
- For subprojects with their own `.cursorrules` (e.g., `relulayer-engine/`, `sbir-digital-twin/`, `sbir-gtm-websites/`), follow those rules when working inside those directories; they specialize but may not override the provenance and parity mandates above.
